    {
      "id": "tutorial-interface-browser-bar-s5",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Check yourself",
      "position": {
        "x": 930,
        "y": 460
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "data": {
        "title": "Check yourself",
        "body": "**Challenge**\n\n1. Open a graph with a `github://` address.\n2. Say what the address is telling you about where the graph lives.\n3. Use refresh, home, or back deliberately instead of guessing.\n4. Reset the view if the zoom indicator says you are far from `1x`.\n5. Explain when you would leave this lesson and open the GitHub material.\n\n**Checkpoint**\n\nYou are done when you can say:\n- the address field tells me what graph I am actually in\n- browser controls are trust and recovery tools\n- bookmarks and zoom help me stay oriented\n- `github://` tells me I am looking at a GitHub-backed artifact\n- GitHub hosting is related, but it is a separate lesson from basic browser-bar literacy",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-interface-browser-bar"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
